Bash(gh pr create --label sandcastle --title "refactor(core): share credential-flag env-var translation across cli" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
Extracts the inline credential-flag-to-env-var mapping that was duplicated verbatim in `bedrock deploy` and `bedrock diff` into a single helper, `buildCredentialOverrides`, in `packages/bedrock/src/cli/credential-environment-overrides.ts`. Both CLI commands now build their `getEnv` overlay on top of the helper.

## Summary

- Add `buildCredentialOverrides({ apiKey?, githubToken? })` that returns `Readonly<Record<string, string>>`, mapping `apiKey` to `BEDROCK_API_KEY` and `githubToken` to `GITHUB_TOKEN`, omitting entries whose flag is `undefined`.
- Replace the inline if-else mapping in `buildGetEnvironment` in both `deploy.ts` and `diff.ts` with a call to the helper.
- Helper is internal (not re-exported from `src/index.ts`) and ready to be reused by the future override spawn-dispatch consumer (PRD #160 user story 16).

Behavior is unchanged: existing deploy and diff tests cover the overlay and process.env fallback paths and continue to pass without modification. Stryker reports 100.00 mutation score on touched files (0 survivors).

